## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "270mA"
  total_current_limit: "270mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "BMEP582040 has NO integrated field I/O on the CPU module — all discrete and analog I/O is provided by separate BME/BMX X80 I/O modules mounted in M580 racks (BMEXBP series); the rack (BMEXBP0400/0800/1200/1600) and at least one power supply module (BMXPSP0400 for 24VDC or BMXPSP0600 for 115-230VAC) MUST be ordered separately; without a rack and power supply the CPU module cannot operate; the CPU occupies slot 00 of the main local rack"
    - "The 2 device network Ethernet ports share a SINGLE IP address via an embedded 2-port switch — do NOT assign different IP addresses to the two ports; the two-port switch supports linear or ring (RSTP) topology but does NOT provide VLAN separation or routing between network segments; for network segmentation between RIO traffic and SCADA traffic, install a BMENOC0311 or BMENOC0321 Ethernet communication module in the rack which provides an additional isolated Ethernet network with its own IP address"
    - "The RIO scanner in the BMEP582040 supports a maximum of 8 remote I/O drops, each with up to 2 X80 racks — exceeding 8 RIO drops requires upgrading to a higher-level M580 CPU (BMEP583020 for 16 drops or BMEP584020 for 31 drops); the RIO network must be on a dedicated Ethernet subnet physically separate from the DIO/SCADA network for deterministic response time; mixing RIO and SCADA traffic on the same switch can cause I/O timeouts and controller watchdog faults"
    - "CIP Safety (SIL2) is integrated in the BMEP582040 but requires specific safety-rated I/O modules (BMESAI0410 etc.) and the EcoStruxure Control Expert Safety programming extension — standard I/O modules cannot be used in safety loops; safety and non-safety tasks must be architecturally isolated per IEC 61508; the safety application requires a separate validation process including FMEA, Safety Requirements Specification, and Factory Acceptance Test; Schneider Electric will not certify a safety application configured only with standard I/O modules"
    - "The expandable flash memory card (BMXRMS004GPF, 4GB) is STRONGLY RECOMMENDED for all production installations — without the memory card, the program is stored only in volatile RAM and a prolonged power failure or CPU replacement will require a full application re-download from the programming PC; the BACKUP LED turns red if the memory card is faulty or absent; hot-swapping the memory card is NOT supported; always power off the rack before inserting or removing the card"
    - "The M580 rack power supply (BMXPSP series) current budget must be calculated before populating modules — each BME/BMX I/O module draws 5V and 24V from the rack backplane; the BMXPSP0400 provides 5V/10A and 24V/0.8A; exceeding the budget causes random module faults and CPU resets; for racks with high analog I/O density or motion modules, a second power supply may be needed on the right side of the rack using a BMXXBE1000 bus extension module"
    - "The Ethernet service port on the BMEP582040 is intended for PROGRAMMING AND MAINTENANCE ONLY — do NOT connect the service port to a production SCADA or historian network; the service port has lower protocol security hardening than the device network ports and is not designed for sustained high-traffic connections; always use the device network ports (Port 1/Port 2) for runtime communications with HMI, SCADA, historians, and remote I/O"
    - "The BMEP582040 is Level 2 in the M580 hierarchy with 8MB program RAM — this limits program size and variable capacity; for large applications with more than 5,000 IEC program organization units, complex function block libraries, or more than 16 remote I/O drops, the BMEP583020 (16MB), BMEP584020 (32MB) or BMEP585040 (128MB) is required; attempting to download an oversized application returns a memory overflow error and the controller will not go to RUN state"
    - "The BMEP582040 requires EcoStruxure Control Expert (formerly Unity Pro) V7.0 minimum for programming — older versions of Unity Pro (V6 and below) do not support the M580 architecture, X80 I/O, or CIP Safety; SoMachine V4.x cannot program M580 CPUs; always verify software compatibility before beginning a migration project from M340 or Premium PLCs to M580, as project migration is not automatic and requires manual re-engineering of hardware configuration and communication variables"
compatibility:
  sw: "EcoStruxure Control Expert V14+ (primary, formerly Unity Pro V14+); Unity Pro V7.0-V13 (legacy); EcoStruxure Control Expert Safety (SIL2 extension); EcoStruxure Operator Terminal Expert; Vijeo SCADA; FactoryTalk not supported (Schneider ecosystem)"
  languages: "Instruction List (IL);Structured Text (ST);Ladder Diagram (LD);Function Block Diagram (FBD);Sequential Function Chart (SFC)"
  frameworks: "IEC61131-3;CIP-Safety-SIL2;Modbus-TCP;EtherNet-IP-scanner-adapter;SNMP;NTP;TFTP;FTP;HTTP;AS-Interface;IEC61508;RSTP"
  certifications: "CE;UL-508;CSA-C22.2-No142;CSA-C22.2-No213-ClassI-Div2;ATEX-II-3-Gas-Dust-Zone2-22;IECEx;EAC-GOST;RCM;EN-IEC-60079;RoHS;REACH;Green-Premium"

